Technical Specification: Spaceware – Proxima Descent (vALPHA)
Horror Game – Rezona Forge Program Entry

• 1. Core Concept

A short horror experience set on Proxima Centauri B. The player controls an astronaut who has just landed. Something is wrong. The planet is not empty.

Genre: Psychological horror / Walking simulator with one threat
Target duration: 3–5 minutes per playthrough
Platform: Rezona (Forge program submission)

• 2. Environment

The scene is the surface of Proxima Centauri B. Black sky, dim red glow from the star. Ground is uneven rock (SVG polygons). A crashed ship behind the player. Fog at the edges of the screen.

No music. Only ambient wind and occasional distant thuds.

• 3. The Threat

One entity. No name. No visible body. It manifests as:

· Flickering lights on the astronaut's suit
· Distorted radio static
· Footstep sounds that do not match the player's movement
· A shadow that appears at the edge of the screen and disappears when looked at

The entity cannot be defeated. It can only be avoided.

• 4. Mechanics

The astronaut moves with joystick (left/right). No jump. No attack. No inventory.

The player must find three scattered data logs to "complete" the mission. Each log is a white dot on the ground. When collected, a text log appears (2-3 sentences of lore).

After collecting the third log, the entity appears directly in front of the player. Screen fades to black. The player wakes up in the ship. The logs are gone. The loop resets.

• 5. Horror Progression

Stage Effect
0 logs collected Normal exploration. Ambient wind. Distant thuds begin.
1 log collected Suit lights flicker occasionally. Static bursts on radio.
2 logs collected Shadow appears at screen edges. Footsteps behind player.
3 logs collected Entity appears. Fade to black. Reset.

• 6. Visual Style

· Black and white only (no color)
· SVG wireframes for all objects (ship, rocks, logs)
· No UI except a subtle counter for logs collected (bottom right, monospace font)
· Screen edges darken slightly as logs are collected

• 7. Audio (Simple)

· Wind loop (low volume)
· Thud sound (every 15-30 seconds, pitch varies randomly)
· Static burst when logs are collected
· Loud distortion when entity appears

• 8. Technical Constraints (Rezona)

· No external assets. All SVG generated by AI from descriptions.
· No complex state beyond log counter and entity appearance flag.
· Joystick only (no buttons S/J/A/I).
· Game resets automatically after entity encounter.

• 9. Success Metrics

· Player completes at least one playthrough (finds all 3 logs)
· Player reports feeling tension or unease
· Playtime between 3-5 minutes
· No crashes or bugs during entity appearance

• 10. Deliverable

A functional Rezona game with:

· Joystick movement (left/right)
· Three collectible data logs on the ground
· Log counter (0/3) in UI
· Ambient wind + random thuds
· Progressive horror effects (flickering lights, static, shadow, footsteps)
· Entity encounter after third log → fade to black → game reset

No combat. No inventory. No crafting. Just exploration and dread.

